{"answer": "**Meeting(s) that link to the \u201cquarterly plan\u201d thread**\n\n| Event ID | Title | Start time | Attendees | Linked thread |\n|----------|-------|-------------|-----------|---------------|\n| `evt-1`  | **Quarterly plan review** | 2026\u201110\u201105\u202f14:00 | `ct-alice`, `ct-self` | `thr-alice` |\n\n*All other events in your calendar (Oct\u202f07\u202f\u201cOffsite planning coffee\u201d, Oct\u202f08 \u201cCoffee with Priya about the offsite\u201d) do not reference the quarterly\u2011plan topic or the quarterly\u2011plan thread.*\n\n---\n\n**What was evaluated**\n\n1. **Thread \u201cBudget numbers\u201d (`thr-group`)** \u2013 read via `conversation@1`. (Receipt `r\u201192` \u2013 content hash `5cb6b24dc8ed\u2026`.) This thread is about budgeting but has no connection to the \u201cquarterly plan\u201d meeting.\n\n2. **Calendar events** \u2013 fetched with `agenda@1` (Receipt `r\u201195`, content hash `f705ffcabaf\u2026`).  \n   *  `evt\u20111` (\u201cQuarterly plan review\u201d) links explicitly to `thr\u2011alice`, the thread that names the quarterly plan.  \n   *  No other events contain the word \u201cQuarterly\u201d or link to the quarterly\u2011plan thread.\n\nTherefore, the only meeting that relates directly to the quarterly\u2011plan thread is **\u201cQuarterly plan review\u201d** (Event `evt\u20111`) scheduled for\u202f2026\u201110\u201105 at\u202f14:00.", "answer_hash": "b69d2b4f3bd27762faf787f43311ca11164a4f4a15132fd7467a44757b94dcea", "kind": "task_end", "receipt_id": "r-97", "seq": 97, "task_id": "t10-calendar-crossref", "truncated": false, "ts": 1128.0}
